WEBVTT

00:00:02.023 --> 00:00:03.454
Previously on Supernatural

00:00:03.772 --> 00:00:04.658
Sammy!

00:00:05.454 --> 00:00:07.635
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can! Go!

00:00:11.632 --> 00:00:12.655
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:13.359 --> 00:00:14.722
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:18.817 --> 00:00:19.817
This is dad's book.

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:21.617
I think he wants us to
pick up where he left off

00:00:22.162 --> 00:00:23.775
Saving people, hunting things.

00:00:23.844 --> 00:00:24.957
Family business.

00:00:25.116 --> 00:00:26.502
Do you think Mom wanted all this for us?

00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:27.706
I can't do this alone.

00:00:28.521 --> 00:00:29.520
I'm driving.

00:01:16.766 --> 00:01:18.379
Can't keep kids out of this place.

00:01:18.629 --> 00:01:19.765
What is it anyway?

00:01:19.901 --> 00:01:21.287
I forgot you're not a local.

00:01:21.446 --> 00:01:22.469
You don't know the legend.

00:01:22.878 --> 00:01:23.650
Legend?

00:01:23.832 --> 00:01:25.768
Every town's got its stories, right?

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:27.836
Ours is Roosevelt asylum.

00:01:28.518 --> 00:01:30.790
They say it's haunted with
the ghosts of the patients.

00:01:31.227 --> 00:01:32.113
Spend the night,

00:01:32.613 --> 00:01:34.340
Spirits will drive you insane.

00:01:40.859 --> 00:01:41.791
Hello?!

00:01:42.222 --> 00:01:43.313
Police officers!

00:01:46.448 --> 00:01:47.812
Police officers!

00:01:56.366 --> 00:01:58.974
You tell me these kids
brought bolt cutters?

00:02:00.092 --> 00:02:00.865
Come on.

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:02.024
Let's split up.

00:02:02.592 --> 00:02:03.523
All right.

00:02:17.724 --> 00:02:18.565
Hello?

00:02:47.516 --> 00:02:48.356
Hello?

00:03:11.964 --> 00:03:12.918
All right.

00:03:13.827 --> 00:03:15.076
Come on out.

00:03:43.491 --> 00:03:44.627
Kelly, you copy?

00:03:46.694 --> 00:03:47.558
Jeez!

00:03:48.376 --> 00:03:49.443
Where the hell you been?!

00:03:49.602 --> 00:03:50.398
In there.

00:03:50.511 --> 00:03:51.647
What was it? See anything?

00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:55.677
No.

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:04.639
This is patrol 1 4. We are
clear, we return to the station

00:04:24.601 --> 00:04:25.351
Hey.

00:04:33.541 --> 00:04:34.540
So, what?

00:04:35.381 --> 00:04:36.812
You're still not talking to me?

00:04:40.018 --> 00:04:40.814
Walt.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:42.927
I said I was sorry about before.

00:04:42.972 --> 00:04:44.722
How many times do I have to say it?

00:05:05.402 --> 00:05:07.856
No, dad was in California
last we heard from him.

00:05:08.424 --> 00:05:11.128
We just thought if he
comes to you for munitions,

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:13.019
Maybe you've seen him
in the last few weeks.

00:05:13.299 --> 00:05:15.046
Just call us if you hear anything. Okay.

00:05:15.195 --> 00:05:16.093
Thanks.

00:05:17.053 --> 00:05:18.151
Caleb hasn't heard from him?

00:05:18.201 --> 00:05:18.874
Nope.

00:05:18.999 --> 00:05:21.244
Neither has Jefferson or pastor Jim.

00:05:21.668 --> 00:05:23.215
What about the journal?
Any leads in there?

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:24.887
No. Same last time I looked.

00:05:24.936 --> 00:05:26.458
Nothing I can make out.

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:30.170
I love the guy, but I swear
he writes like freaking Yoda.

00:05:30.171 --> 00:05:31.667
And maybe we should call the feds,

00:05:31.817 --> 00:05:32.865
File a missing person's out.

00:05:32.866 --> 00:05:35.260
We talked about this. Dad would be
pissed if we put the feds on his tail.

00:05:35.261 --> 00:05:36.407
I don't care anymore

00:05:36.532 --> 00:05:38.550
After all that happened back in kansas,

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:39.573
I mean...

00:05:39.823 --> 00:05:40.771
He should have been there, Dean.

00:05:40.772 --> 00:05:42.791
You said so yourself. You
tried to call him and nothing.

00:05:42.866 --> 00:05:43.864
I know.

00:05:44.311 --> 00:05:45.658
I loose my cellphone.

00:05:45.758 --> 00:05:47.604
You know, he could be
dead for all we know.

00:05:47.605 --> 00:05:48.876
Don't say that.

00:05:49.201 --> 00:05:50.723
He's not dead. He's...

00:05:50.822 --> 00:05:53.118
He's what? He's hiding? He's busy?

00:05:59.579 --> 00:06:00.776
I don't believe it.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:02.323
What?

00:06:06.070 --> 00:06:08.016
It's a-A text message.

00:06:09.213 --> 00:06:10.336
It's coordinates.

00:06:12.381 --> 00:06:14.253
You think dad was texting us?

00:06:14.449 --> 00:06:15.747
He's given us coordinates before.

00:06:15.797 --> 00:06:17.867
The man can barely work a toaster, Dean.

00:06:18.092 --> 00:06:19.439
Sam, this is good news.

00:06:19.539 --> 00:06:20.936
It means he's okay, or alive.

00:06:21.136 --> 00:06:22.757
Was there a number on the caller I.D.?

00:06:22.807 --> 00:06:24.005
Huh, it said "unknown."

00:06:24.060 --> 00:06:25.332
Okay, well, where do
the coordinates point?

00:06:25.382 --> 00:06:26.655
That's the interesting part.

00:06:26.854 --> 00:06:28.301
Rockford, Illinois.

00:06:29.271 --> 00:06:30.469
Okay, and that's interesting how?

00:06:30.519 --> 00:06:33.313
I checked the local rockford
paper. Take a look at this.

00:06:36.678 --> 00:06:38.275
This cop, Walter Kelly,

00:06:38.499 --> 00:06:40.371
Comes home from his
shift, shoots his wife,

00:06:40.495 --> 00:06:42.541
Then puts the gun in his
mouth, blows his brains out.

00:06:42.641 --> 00:06:44.736
Earlier that night,
kelly and his partner

00:06:44.737 --> 00:06:47.294
Responded to a call at
the Roosevelt asylum.

00:06:47.369 --> 00:06:49.888
Okay, I'm not following. What
does this have to do with us?

00:06:49.889 --> 00:06:52.832
Dad earmarked the same
asylum in the journal.

00:06:53.603 --> 00:06:54.851
Let's see.

00:06:56.472 --> 00:06:57.171
Here.

00:06:57.246 --> 00:06:59.890
"Seven unconfirmed
sightings, two deaths"

00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:01.487
Till last week, at least.

00:07:01.761 --> 00:07:03.556
I think this is where he wants us to go.

00:07:07.307 --> 00:07:08.429
This is a job.

00:07:10.275 --> 00:07:11.473
Dad wants us to work a job.

00:07:11.548 --> 00:07:13.244
Maybe we'll meet up with
him. Maybe he's there.

00:07:13.245 --> 00:07:14.317
Maybe he's not.

00:07:14.489 --> 00:07:16.560
May He could be sending us there
by ourselves to hunting thing.

00:07:16.561 --> 00:07:17.872
Who cares?

00:07:18.581 --> 00:07:20.477
If he wants us there,
it's good enough for me.

00:07:20.801 --> 00:07:22.523
This doesn't strike you as weird...

00:07:23.521 --> 00:07:24.494
The texting,

00:07:24.741 --> 00:07:26.013
The coordinates? Sam.

00:07:26.388 --> 00:07:28.533
Dad's telling us to go
somewhere. We're going.

00:07:49.517 --> 00:07:51.513
You're Daniel Gunderson,
right, you're cop?

00:07:51.688 --> 00:07:52.461
Yeah.

00:07:53.484 --> 00:07:54.332
I'm...

00:07:54.405 --> 00:07:55.677
Nigel Tufnel

00:07:55.727 --> 00:07:56.849
With the chicago tribune.

00:07:56.850 --> 00:07:58.396
Do you mind if I ask a couple questions

00:07:58.397 --> 00:07:59.444
About your partner?

00:07:59.445 --> 00:08:00.392
Yeah, I do.

00:08:00.393 --> 00:08:01.365
I'm just trying to have a beer here.

00:08:01.366 --> 00:08:03.685
I just want to hear
the story in your words.

00:08:04.293 --> 00:08:06.363
A week ago, my partner
was sitting in that chair,

00:08:06.762 --> 00:08:07.910
And now he's dead.

00:08:08.010 --> 00:08:09.157
Are you gonna ambush me here?

00:08:09.158 --> 00:08:09.931
Sorry,

00:08:09.932 --> 00:08:11.527
But I need to know what happened.

00:08:11.652 --> 00:08:14.421
Heyn buddy! How about leaving
the poor guy alone, huh?!

00:08:14.755 --> 00:08:17.200
The man's an officer! Why don't
you show a little respect?!

00:08:24.408 --> 00:08:25.531
You didn't have to do that.

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:26.903
Yeah, of course I did.

00:08:27.635 --> 00:08:28.932
That guy's a serious jerk.

00:08:29.157 --> 00:08:31.028
Let me buy you a beer, huh?

00:08:31.701 --> 00:08:32.699
Two?

00:08:36.317 --> 00:08:37.090
Thanks.

00:08:42.156 --> 00:08:43.603
You shoved me kind of
hard in there, buddy boy.

00:08:43.628 --> 00:08:45.125
I had to sell it, didn't I?

00:08:45.774 --> 00:08:46.971
It's method acting.

00:08:48.019 --> 00:08:48.842
Huh?

00:08:49.339 --> 00:08:50.112
Never mind.

00:08:50.113 --> 00:08:51.235
What did you find out from Gunderson?

00:08:51.335 --> 00:08:53.006
So, Walter Kelly was a good cop.

00:08:53.231 --> 00:08:54.827
Head of his class, even-Keeled.

00:08:54.877 --> 00:08:56.224
He had a bright future ahead of him.

00:08:56.225 --> 00:08:56.873
What about at home?

00:08:56.874 --> 00:08:58.842
He and his wife had a few
fights. Like everybody.

00:08:58.892 --> 00:09:00.364
But it was mostly smooth sailing.

00:09:00.514 --> 00:09:02.110
They were even talking
about having kids.

00:09:02.111 --> 00:09:04.854
All right, so how the kelly had some
deep see the crazy way in the bus

00:09:04.855 --> 00:09:06.227
Or something else did it to him. Right.

00:09:06.324 --> 00:09:08.070
What did Gunderson tell
you about the asylum?

00:09:09.193 --> 00:09:09.891
A lot.

00:09:34.913 --> 00:09:37.632
So, apparently, the cops
chased the kids here...

00:09:39.451 --> 00:09:40.973
Into the south wing.

00:09:43.044 --> 00:09:44.216
South wing, huh?

00:09:44.834 --> 00:09:46.356
Wait a second.

00:09:47.579 --> 00:09:49.475
South wing, south wing.

00:09:52.493 --> 00:09:54.015
"1972,

00:09:54.215 --> 00:09:56.076
Three kids broke into the south wing.

00:09:56.201 --> 00:09:57.673
Only one survived."

00:09:57.872 --> 00:09:59.167
The way he tells it, one of his friends

00:09:59.168 --> 00:10:01.138
Went nuts and started
lighting up the place.

00:10:02.061 --> 00:10:03.707
So, whatever's going on,

00:10:03.882 --> 00:10:05.354
South wing seems like the heart of it.

00:10:05.404 --> 00:10:06.976
Yeah, but if kids are
spelunking the asylum,

00:10:06.977 --> 00:10:08.793
Why aren't there a ton more deaths?

00:10:10.789 --> 00:10:12.710
It looks like the doors
are usually chained.

00:10:13.758 --> 00:10:15.430
They could have been
chained up for years.

00:10:15.923 --> 00:10:17.670
Yeah, to keep people out.

00:10:18.318 --> 00:10:19.965
Or to keep something in.

00:10:30.319 --> 00:10:32.664
Let me know if you see any
dead people, Haley Joel.

00:10:32.814 --> 00:10:33.936
Dude, enough.

00:10:34.834 --> 00:10:36.553
I'm serious. You've got
to be careful. Right.

00:10:36.554 --> 00:10:38.748
Ghosts are attracted to
that E.S.P. Thing you got.

00:10:38.749 --> 00:10:39.946
I told you, it's not E.S.P.

00:10:39.947 --> 00:10:42.166
I just have strange vibes, sometimes,

00:10:42.765 --> 00:10:43.439
Weird dreams.

00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:45.352
Yeah, whatever. Don't ask, don't tell.

00:10:45.577 --> 00:10:46.974
Do you get any reading
on that thing or not?

00:10:47.049 --> 00:10:48.970
No. Of course, it doesn't
mean nobody's home.

00:10:49.045 --> 00:10:51.290
Spirits can't appear
during certain hours of day.

00:10:51.315 --> 00:10:52.785
The freaks come out at night.

00:10:53.009 --> 00:10:53.982
Ya. Hey Sam

00:10:54.032 --> 00:10:55.554
Who do you think is a hotter psychic

00:10:55.629 --> 00:10:57.675
Patricia Arquette,
Jennifer Love Hewitt or you?

00:11:24.648 --> 00:11:25.621
Man.

00:11:26.869 --> 00:11:28.216
Electroshock,

00:11:28.390 --> 00:11:31.032
Lobotomies. They did some
twisted stuff to these people,

00:11:31.257 --> 00:11:34.175
Kind of like my man
Jack in "cuckoo's nest."

00:11:38.063 --> 00:11:39.884
So, what do you think?

00:11:40.533 --> 00:11:42.154
Ghosts are possessing people?

00:11:42.803 --> 00:11:43.676
Maybe.

00:11:44.524 --> 00:11:47.518
Maybe it's more like Amityville
or the smurl haunting.

00:11:47.714 --> 00:11:50.010
Ah, spirits driving them insane,

00:11:50.633 --> 00:11:52.779
Kind of like my man
Jack in "the shining."

00:11:56.521 --> 00:11:57.491
Dean...

00:11:59.462 --> 00:12:00.585
When are we going to talk about it?

00:12:00.685 --> 00:12:01.333
Talk about what?

00:12:01.358 --> 00:12:02.955
About the fact that dad's not here.

00:12:03.130 --> 00:12:05.076
Oh, uh, let's see, never.

00:12:05.077 --> 00:12:06.024
I'm being serious, man.

00:12:06.025 --> 00:12:06.851
So am I, sam.

00:12:06.852 --> 00:12:09.321
Look. He sent us here. He
obviously wants us here.

00:12:09.520 --> 00:12:10.643
We'll just have to pick
up the search later.

00:12:10.644 --> 00:12:12.215
It doesn't matter what he wants.

00:12:12.216 --> 00:12:14.556
See, that attitude right there,

00:12:15.055 --> 00:12:16.577
That is why I always
got the extra cookie.

00:12:16.701 --> 00:12:17.799
Dad could be in trouble.

00:12:17.874 --> 00:12:19.396
We should be looking for him.

00:12:19.421 --> 00:12:22.240
We deserve some answers, Dean. I mean,
this is our family were talking about..

00:12:22.241 --> 00:12:23.659
I understand that, sam,

00:12:23.809 --> 00:12:24.831
But he's given us an order.

00:12:24.832 --> 00:12:26.528
So what ? We've got to
always follow dad's orders?

00:12:26.553 --> 00:12:27.875
Of course we do.

00:12:38.896 --> 00:12:40.643
Sanford Ellicott

00:12:41.865 --> 00:12:42.888
You know what we got to do?

00:12:43.013 --> 00:12:45.103
We've got to find out
more about the south wing,

00:12:45.630 --> 00:12:47.177
See if something happened here.

00:13:03.730 --> 00:13:04.778
Sam Winchester?

00:13:05.826 --> 00:13:06.575
That's me.

00:13:06.649 --> 00:13:07.647
Come on in.

00:13:13.953 --> 00:13:16.351
Thanks again for see me last minute.

00:13:31.495 --> 00:13:32.593
Dr. Ellicott?

00:13:33.413 --> 00:13:34.611
Ellicott, that name.

00:13:34.885 --> 00:13:37.929
Wasn't there a dr. Sanford Ellicott?

00:13:38.328 --> 00:13:40.947
Yeah, he was a chief
psychiatrist somewhere.

00:13:40.948 --> 00:13:43.989
My father was chief of staff
at the old Roosevelt asylum.

00:13:44.114 --> 00:13:45.162
How did you know?

00:13:45.785 --> 00:13:48.829
Huh, well, I'm sort of
a local-History buff.

00:13:48.976 --> 00:13:52.768
Hey, wasn't there an incident
or something in the...

00:13:52.968 --> 00:13:54.864
In the hospital, I guess,
in the south wing, right?

00:13:54.913 --> 00:13:56.435
We're on your dollar, Sam.

00:13:57.251 --> 00:13:58.873
We're here to talk about you.

00:13:59.796 --> 00:14:01.867
Oh, okay, yeah, yeah, sure.

00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:04.733
So? So.

00:14:04.858 --> 00:14:06.005
How's things?

00:14:06.205 --> 00:14:08.550
Uh, things are good, doctor.

00:14:08.600 --> 00:14:09.448
Good.

00:14:09.648 --> 00:14:10.895
What you been doing?

00:14:11.741 --> 00:14:12.863
Uh...

00:14:13.487 --> 00:14:15.632
Same old. I've just been on a...

00:14:15.707 --> 00:14:17.728
On a road trip with my brother.

00:14:17.803 --> 00:14:19.025
Was that fun?

00:14:21.094 --> 00:14:22.116
Loads.

00:14:22.665 --> 00:14:23.763
Um...

00:14:24.137 --> 00:14:25.310
You know... We...

00:14:26.507 --> 00:14:27.954
Met a lot of...

00:14:28.703 --> 00:14:29.825
Interesting people.

00:14:29.875 --> 00:14:30.624
Mm-Hmm.

00:14:30.775 --> 00:14:32.297
Did a lot of, uh...

00:14:33.394 --> 00:14:34.991
A lot of interesting things.

00:14:35.814 --> 00:14:36.937
Uh...

00:14:38.010 --> 00:14:38.958
You know,

00:14:39.332 --> 00:14:40.430
What was it...

00:14:40.494 --> 00:14:42.415
Exactly that happened in the south wing?

00:14:42.465 --> 00:14:43.413
I forget... Look,

00:14:43.563 --> 00:14:44.960
If you're a local-History buff,

00:14:45.007 --> 00:14:47.003
Then you know all about
the Roosevelt riot.

00:14:47.353 --> 00:14:48.101
The riot?

00:14:48.126 --> 00:14:50.346
Well, no, I know, I'm
just curious -- Sam.

00:14:51.095 --> 00:14:52.517
Let's cut the bull, shall we?

00:14:53.263 --> 00:14:54.760
You're avoiding the subject.

00:14:57.953 --> 00:14:58.852
What subject?

00:14:58.951 --> 00:14:59.800
You.

00:15:00.423 --> 00:15:02.020
Now, I'll make you a deal.

00:15:02.691 --> 00:15:04.886
I'll tell you all
about the Roosevelt riot

00:15:05.061 --> 00:15:07.456
If you tell me something
honest about yourself...

00:15:08.129 --> 00:15:09.152
Like, uh...

00:15:09.748 --> 00:15:11.744
This brother you're road-Tripping with.

00:15:12.243 --> 00:15:13.715
How do you feel about him?

00:15:25.450 --> 00:15:25.974
Dude.

00:15:26.074 --> 00:15:28.219
You were in there forever. What
the hell were you talking about?

00:15:28.566 --> 00:15:29.764
Just the hospital, you know.

00:15:29.838 --> 00:15:30.562
And?

00:15:30.637 --> 00:15:32.308
And the south wing,

00:15:32.408 --> 00:15:33.930
It's where they housed
the real hard cases,

00:15:33.980 --> 00:15:35.776
Psychotics, the criminally insane.

00:15:35.823 --> 00:15:36.572
Sounds cozy.

00:15:36.597 --> 00:15:38.842
Yeah, and one night in '64, they rioted,

00:15:39.041 --> 00:15:40.962
Attacked the staff, attacked each other.

00:15:41.037 --> 00:15:42.609
So, what, the patients
took over the asylum?

00:15:42.756 --> 00:15:44.278
Apparently. Any deaths?

00:15:44.578 --> 00:15:46.524
Some patients, some staff.

00:15:46.648 --> 00:15:47.796
I guess it was pretty gory.

00:15:47.797 --> 00:15:49.542
Some of the bodies were
never even recovered,

00:15:49.642 --> 00:15:51.663
Including our chief of staff, Ellicott.

00:15:51.664 --> 00:15:52.935
What do you mean "Never recovered"?

00:15:52.963 --> 00:15:54.286
Cops scoured every inch of the place,

00:15:54.336 --> 00:15:56.207
But I guess the patients must have...

00:15:57.354 --> 00:15:59.625
Stuffed the bodies somewhere hidden.

00:15:59.996 --> 00:16:01.094
That's grim. Ya.

00:16:01.568 --> 00:16:03.738
So they transferred all
the surviving patients

00:16:03.739 --> 00:16:05.285
And shut down the hospital for good.

00:16:05.286 --> 00:16:08.275
All right so the * we've got a bunch of
violent deaths and unrecovered bodies.

00:16:08.276 --> 00:16:09.821
Which could mean a
bunch of angry spirits.

00:16:10.096 --> 00:16:12.404
Not good times. Let's check
out the hospital tonight.

00:16:33.127 --> 00:16:34.574
Check this out.

00:16:35.796 --> 00:16:36.769
Creepy...

00:16:38.571 --> 00:16:39.868
Yet terrifying.

00:16:41.739 --> 00:16:43.361
I thought we were going to a movie.

00:16:44.009 --> 00:16:45.881
This is better. It's
like we're in a movie.

00:16:47.774 --> 00:16:49.545
I can't believe you call this a date.

00:16:52.436 --> 00:16:53.858
Come on. That'll be fine.

00:16:54.407 --> 00:16:55.729
That's look around.

00:16:56.328 --> 00:16:57.500
Come on!

00:17:04.461 --> 00:17:05.484
What was that? Ugh!

00:17:09.077 --> 00:17:10.075
Hey, look.

00:17:10.297 --> 00:17:11.719
Come on, let's check it out.

00:17:12.093 --> 00:17:13.540
I don't want to.

00:17:14.314 --> 00:17:15.037
Let's just go.

00:17:15.087 --> 00:17:16.359
Come on.

00:17:19.136 --> 00:17:20.059
Okay.

00:17:20.433 --> 00:17:21.656
Okay. You can wait here.

00:17:21.756 --> 00:17:23.003
Gavin, no.

00:17:23.103 --> 00:17:24.325
I'm just gonna be a minute.

00:17:25.772 --> 00:17:27.693
Nothing's gonna get you, I promise.

00:18:20.496 --> 00:18:21.469
Damn it.

00:18:25.541 --> 00:18:27.761
Hey, sweetie, couldn't take it, huh?

00:18:32.125 --> 00:18:32.998
Hey.

00:18:37.813 --> 00:18:40.033
Gavin, where are you?

00:18:42.411 --> 00:18:43.434
Gavin.

00:19:12.518 --> 00:19:13.641
Getting readings?

00:19:14.140 --> 00:19:15.137
No, big-Time.

00:19:15.362 --> 00:19:17.358
This place is orbing like crazy.

00:19:21.347 --> 00:19:23.393
There's probably multiple
spirits out and about.

00:19:23.439 --> 00:19:25.884
And if these unrecovered
bodies are causing the haunting?

00:19:25.885 --> 00:19:27.205
We got to find them and burn them.

00:19:27.255 --> 00:19:27.986
Just be careful.

00:19:27.987 --> 00:19:30.959
The only thing that makes me more
nervous than a pissed-Off spirit

00:19:31.446 --> 00:19:34.217
Is a pissed-Off spirit
of a psycho killer.

00:20:45.166 --> 00:20:45.901
Dean!

00:20:46.636 --> 00:20:47.258
Dean!

00:20:48.050 --> 00:20:48.870
Shotgun!

00:20:49.520 --> 00:20:50.341
Sam, get down!

00:21:00.425 --> 00:21:01.415
That was weird.

00:21:01.613 --> 00:21:02.320
Yeah,

00:21:02.715 --> 00:21:03.592
You're telling me.

00:21:05.571 --> 00:21:08.286
No, Dean, I mean, it was weird
that she didn't attack me.

00:21:08.377 --> 00:21:10.186
It looked pretty aggro
from where I was standing.

00:21:10.187 --> 00:21:11.431
She didn't hurt me.

00:21:11.515 --> 00:21:12.703
She didn't even try.

00:21:13.105 --> 00:21:15.452
So she didn't want to hurt
me, then what did she want?

00:21:44.512 --> 00:21:45.983
It's all right.We're
not going to hurt you.

00:21:47.821 --> 00:21:48.895
It's okay.

00:21:49.778 --> 00:21:50.457
What's your name?

00:21:50.485 --> 00:21:51.277
Katherine.

00:21:52.578 --> 00:21:53.454
Kat.

00:21:53.624 --> 00:21:54.359
Okay.

00:21:54.614 --> 00:21:55.660
I'm dean.This is sam.

00:21:55.661 --> 00:21:56.904
What are you doing here?

00:21:58.215 --> 00:22:00.025
My boyfriend, Gavin...

00:22:00.308 --> 00:22:01.354
Is he here?

00:22:01.954 --> 00:22:03.057
Somewhere.

00:22:03.735 --> 00:22:06.676
He thought it would be fun,
try and see some ghosts.

00:22:07.468 --> 00:22:09.193
I thought it was all just...

00:22:10.075 --> 00:22:11.065
You know...

00:22:11.800 --> 00:22:12.931
Pretend.

00:22:15.900 --> 00:22:17.003
I've seen things.

00:22:18.537 --> 00:22:20.431
I heard Gavin scream, and...

00:22:20.516 --> 00:22:22.184
All right, Kat, come on.

00:22:22.524 --> 00:22:24.446
Sam's gonna get you out of here.
Then we're gonna find your boyfriend.

00:22:24.464 --> 00:22:26.076
No, no.

00:22:27.179 --> 00:22:29.130
I'm not gonna leave without Gavin.

00:22:29.385 --> 00:22:30.685
I'm coming with you.

00:22:30.686 --> 00:22:32.728
It's no a joke around
here, okay. It's dangerous.

00:22:32.813 --> 00:22:34.509
That's why I've got to find him.

00:22:36.149 --> 00:22:37.846
All right, I guess we're
gonna split up, then.

00:22:38.096 --> 00:22:39.029
Let's go.

00:22:43.327 --> 00:22:44.401
Gavin!

00:22:48.000 --> 00:22:48.990
Gavin!

00:22:52.157 --> 00:22:53.118
Gavin!

00:22:55.720 --> 00:22:56.738
Gavin!

00:22:57.112 --> 00:22:58.497
I've got a question for you.

00:22:58.893 --> 00:23:00.816
You've seen a lot of
horror movies, yeah?

00:23:01.042 --> 00:23:01.834
I guess so.

00:23:01.835 --> 00:23:03.700
Do me a favor. Next time you see one,

00:23:03.870 --> 00:23:04.916
Pay attention.

00:23:05.351 --> 00:23:06.963
When someone says a place is haunted,

00:23:07.246 --> 00:23:08.349
Don't go in.

00:23:23.112 --> 00:23:23.875
Gavin?

00:23:24.497 --> 00:23:25.600
Hey, gavin.

00:23:26.477 --> 00:23:28.626
Hey, it's okay. It's
okay. I'm here to help.

00:23:29.333 --> 00:23:30.039
Who are you?

00:23:30.040 --> 00:23:31.375
My name is Sam.

00:23:31.884 --> 00:23:33.213
We found your girlfriend.

00:23:33.694 --> 00:23:34.571
Kat? Yeah.

00:23:34.572 --> 00:23:35.730
Is she all right?

00:23:35.934 --> 00:23:38.151
She's worried about you. Are you okay?

00:23:39.821 --> 00:23:41.484
I was running. I, uh,

00:23:41.614 --> 00:23:42.690
I think I fell.

00:23:42.691 --> 00:23:44.060
You were running from what?

00:23:45.854 --> 00:23:47.060
There was...

00:23:47.582 --> 00:23:50.328
There was this girl. Her-Her face...

00:23:51.925 --> 00:23:53.067
It was all messed up.

00:23:53.068 --> 00:23:54.110
Okay, listen, listen,

00:23:54.111 --> 00:23:56.099
This girl, did she try to hurt you?

00:23:56.726 --> 00:23:58.780
What? No, she, uh...

00:23:59.595 --> 00:24:00.867
She what?

00:24:02.041 --> 00:24:03.215
She kissed me.

00:24:05.700 --> 00:24:08.537
Um, but she didn't hurt you physically?

00:24:08.732 --> 00:24:10.656
Dude, she kissed me.

00:24:11.308 --> 00:24:12.482
I'm scarred for life.

00:24:13.760 --> 00:24:15.358
Trust me, it could have been worse.

00:24:15.359 --> 00:24:17.021
And now, do you remember anything else?

00:24:17.445 --> 00:24:18.619
She, uh...

00:24:19.467 --> 00:24:21.423
Actually, she tried to
whisper something in my ear.

00:24:22.050 --> 00:24:22.930
What?

00:24:23.745 --> 00:24:25.278
I don't know. I ran like hell.

00:24:39.991 --> 00:24:41.915
You son of a bitch.

00:24:42.697 --> 00:24:44.556
It's all right. I've got a lighter.

00:24:47.674 --> 00:24:49.663
Ow. You're hurting my arm.

00:24:50.674 --> 00:24:51.881
What are you talking about?

00:25:00.681 --> 00:25:03.355
Let me out!Please!

00:25:08.270 --> 00:25:10.433
Kat, hang on!

00:25:38.039 --> 00:25:38.985
What's going on?

00:25:38.986 --> 00:25:40.142
She's inside with one of them.

00:25:40.143 --> 00:25:41.382
Help me!

00:25:41.447 --> 00:25:42.197
Kat!

00:25:42.198 --> 00:25:43.469
Get me out of here!

00:25:43.470 --> 00:25:45.381
Kat, it's not gonna hurt you.

00:25:45.903 --> 00:25:48.544
Listen to me. You have to
face it. You have to calm down.

00:25:48.545 --> 00:25:49.693
She's got to what?

00:25:49.694 --> 00:25:50.606
I have to what?

00:25:50.607 --> 00:25:53.443
These spirits, they don't try to
hurt, they're trying to communicate.

00:25:53.444 --> 00:25:55.041
You've got to listen to.
You've got to face it.

00:25:55.042 --> 00:25:55.986
You face it.

00:25:55.987 --> 00:25:57.617
No. It's the only way you're
gonna get out of there.

00:25:57.618 --> 00:25:58.398
No!

00:25:58.399 --> 00:25:59.572
Look at it.That's all.

00:25:59.637 --> 00:26:00.974
Come on.You can do it.

00:26:22.522 --> 00:26:23.272
Kat?

00:26:25.164 --> 00:26:26.794
Now, I hope you're right about this.

00:26:28.791 --> 00:26:29.998
Yeah, me, too.

00:26:39.924 --> 00:26:41.065
Oh, Kat.

00:26:46.289 --> 00:26:47.659
1, 3, 7.

00:26:48.409 --> 00:26:49.452
Sorry?

00:26:50.789 --> 00:26:52.420
It whispered in my ear

00:26:52.811 --> 00:26:53.952
1, 3, 7.

00:26:54.937 --> 00:26:56.404
Room number.

00:26:59.698 --> 00:27:02.259
All right. So if these spirits
aren't trying to hurt anyone.

00:27:02.260 --> 00:27:03.825
Then what are they trying to do?

00:27:04.151 --> 00:27:05.423
Maybe that's what they've
been trying to tell us.

00:27:05.424 --> 00:27:06.564
I guess we'll find out.

00:27:07.249 --> 00:27:08.194
All right.

00:27:10.842 --> 00:27:11.723
So,

00:27:11.724 --> 00:27:13.940
Now, you guys ready to leave this place?

00:27:14.462 --> 00:27:15.669
That's an understatement.

00:27:15.702 --> 00:27:16.712
Okay.

00:27:17.136 --> 00:27:18.539
You get them out of here.

00:27:18.740 --> 00:27:20.469
I'm gonna gofind room 137.

00:27:29.438 --> 00:27:32.307
So, how do you guys know
about all this ghost stuff?

00:27:33.547 --> 00:27:35.405
It's kind of our job.

00:27:36.455 --> 00:27:38.412
Why would anyone want a job like that?

00:27:40.825 --> 00:27:42.944
I had a crappy guidance counselor.

00:27:45.201 --> 00:27:47.418
And Dean? He's your boss?

00:27:49.733 --> 00:27:50.614
No.

00:28:34.730 --> 00:28:35.740
All right.

00:28:36.001 --> 00:28:37.632
I think we have a small problem.

00:28:38.217 --> 00:28:39.260
Let's break it down.

00:28:39.423 --> 00:28:40.434
I don't think that's gonna work.

00:28:40.564 --> 00:28:41.445
Then a window.

00:28:41.446 --> 00:28:42.097
They're barred.

00:28:42.098 --> 00:28:43.793
How are we supposed to get out?

00:28:45.782 --> 00:28:47.510
That's the point. We're not.

00:28:48.071 --> 00:28:49.376
There's something in here.

00:28:49.506 --> 00:28:50.712
It doesn't want us to leave.

00:28:53.060 --> 00:28:53.941
Those patients.

00:28:54.006 --> 00:28:54.952
No.

00:28:55.473 --> 00:28:56.582
Something else.

00:29:22.340 --> 00:29:24.851
This is why I get paid the big bucks.

00:29:31.400 --> 00:29:32.737
"Patients journal."

00:29:48.934 --> 00:29:51.542
All work and no play makes Dr. Ellicott,

00:29:51.680 --> 00:29:53.669
A very dull boy.

00:30:01.601 --> 00:30:03.390
Right. I've looked everywhere.

00:30:03.672 --> 00:30:04.767
There's no other way out.

00:30:05.143 --> 00:30:06.128
So, what the hell are we gonna do?

00:30:06.191 --> 00:30:07.745
For starters, we're not gonna panic.

00:30:07.885 --> 00:30:08.949
Why the hell not?

00:30:11.484 --> 00:30:12.110
Hey.

00:30:12.157 --> 00:30:13.189
Sam, it's me.

00:30:13.659 --> 00:30:15.364
I see it. It's coming at me.

00:30:15.682 --> 00:30:16.401
Where are you?

00:30:16.402 --> 00:30:17.481
I'm in the basement. Hurry up!

00:30:17.512 --> 00:30:18.420
I'm on my way.

00:30:18.670 --> 00:30:20.751
All right. Can either
of you handle a shotgun?

00:30:21.158 --> 00:30:22.112
What?! No!

00:30:22.566 --> 00:30:23.270
I can.

00:30:24.980 --> 00:30:26.763
My dad took me skeet
shooting a couple times.

00:30:26.810 --> 00:30:27.655
Oh, I heard.

00:30:27.796 --> 00:30:28.828
It's loaded with rock salt.

00:30:28.875 --> 00:30:29.845
Now, it might not kill a spirit,

00:30:29.892 --> 00:30:31.394
But it will repel it,
so if you see something,

00:30:31.551 --> 00:30:32.051
Shoot.

00:30:32.067 --> 00:30:32.724
Okay.

00:30:32.959 --> 00:30:33.569
Okay.

00:30:40.286 --> 00:30:41.083
Dean!

00:30:59.655 --> 00:31:00.515
Dean!

00:32:01.622 --> 00:32:02.452
Dean?

00:32:30.013 --> 00:32:31.296
Don't be afraid.

00:32:31.640 --> 00:32:33.142
I'm going to make you all better.

00:32:40.447 --> 00:32:41.495
Hey, Gavin.

00:32:43.237 --> 00:32:43.941
Yeah?

00:32:45.677 --> 00:32:47.398
If we make it out of here alive,

00:32:48.587 --> 00:32:50.105
We are so breaking up.

00:32:53.544 --> 00:32:54.592
Did you hear that?

00:32:54.764 --> 00:32:55.828
Something's coming.

00:32:59.489 --> 00:33:00.882
Damn it! Damn it! Damn it!

00:33:01.492 --> 00:33:02.822
Don't shoot! It's me!

00:33:03.072 --> 00:33:04.735
Sorry. Sorry.

00:33:05.314 --> 00:33:06.581
Son of a...

00:33:10.915 --> 00:33:12.167
What are you still doing here?

00:33:12.438 --> 00:33:13.392
Where's Sam?

00:33:13.705 --> 00:33:15.144
He went to the basement. You called him.

00:33:15.989 --> 00:33:16.787
I didn't call him.

00:33:16.917 --> 00:33:18.043
His cellphone rang.

00:33:18.340 --> 00:33:19.295
He said it was you.

00:33:21.329 --> 00:33:22.314
Basement, huh?

00:33:26.630 --> 00:33:27.474
All right.

00:33:28.585 --> 00:33:29.571
Watch yourselves.

00:33:31.761 --> 00:33:32.856
And watch out for me.

00:33:39.080 --> 00:33:39.878
Sammy?

00:33:41.615 --> 00:33:42.866
Sam, you down here?

00:33:43.758 --> 00:33:44.572
Sam!

00:33:47.075 --> 00:33:47.971
Sam!

00:33:50.303 --> 00:33:51.038
Man...

00:33:51.820 --> 00:33:53.432
Answer me when I'm calling you.

00:33:53.995 --> 00:33:54.574
You all right?

00:33:54.575 --> 00:33:55.638
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:33:55.779 --> 00:33:57.202
You know that wasn't
me who called, right?

00:33:57.300 --> 00:33:59.286
Yeah, I know. I think
something lured me down here.

00:33:59.287 --> 00:34:00.648
I think I know who

00:34:00.867 --> 00:34:01.727
Dr. Ellicott.

00:34:02.169 --> 00:34:04.375
That's what the spirits have been trying
to tell us. You haven't seen him, have you?

00:34:04.469 --> 00:34:05.283
No.

00:34:05.471 --> 00:34:06.425
How do you knowit was him?

00:34:06.426 --> 00:34:07.770
Because I found his logbook.

00:34:07.802 --> 00:34:10.336
Apparently, he was
experimenting on his patients.

00:34:10.826 --> 00:34:11.952
Awful stuff.

00:34:11.983 --> 00:34:13.658
Makes lobotomies look
like a couple of aspirin.

00:34:13.659 --> 00:34:15.300
But it was the patients who rioted.

00:34:15.301 --> 00:34:17.053
Yeah. They were rioting
against Dr. Ellicott.

00:34:18.304 --> 00:34:21.782
Dr. Feelgood was working on some
sort of extreme-Rage therapy.

00:34:21.783 --> 00:34:24.113
He thought if he could get his
patients to vent their anger,

00:34:24.223 --> 00:34:25.506
Then they'd be cured of it.

00:34:25.897 --> 00:34:27.196
Instead it only made
them worse and worse

00:34:27.197 --> 00:34:28.447
And angrier and angrier.

00:34:28.651 --> 00:34:30.090
I'm thinking, what if his spirit

00:34:30.309 --> 00:34:31.529
Is doing the same thing?

00:34:31.764 --> 00:34:32.531
To the cop,

00:34:32.645 --> 00:34:34.022
The kids in the '70s

00:34:34.335 --> 00:34:36.697
Making them so angry
they become homicidal.

00:34:37.777 --> 00:34:38.449
Come on.

00:34:38.731 --> 00:34:40.421
We've got to find his
bones and torch them.

00:34:40.921 --> 00:34:41.766
How?

00:34:42.086 --> 00:34:43.400
The police never found his body.

00:34:43.462 --> 00:34:46.185
The logbook said he had some
hidden procedure room down here

00:34:46.186 --> 00:34:48.328
Somewhere where he'd
work on his patients. So,

00:34:48.474 --> 00:34:50.273
If I was a patient, I'd
drag his ass down here

00:34:50.274 --> 00:34:51.634
Do a little work on myself.

00:34:51.681 --> 00:34:53.089
I don't know.It sounds kind of...

00:34:53.152 --> 00:34:53.871
Of crazy?

00:34:53.872 --> 00:34:54.387
Yeah.

00:34:54.388 --> 00:34:55.858
Yeah, exactly.

00:35:11.858 --> 00:35:13.110
I told you I looked everywhere.

00:35:13.111 --> 00:35:14.815
I didn't find a hidden room.

00:35:15.191 --> 00:35:16.771
Well, that's why they call it hidden.

00:35:19.701 --> 00:35:20.765
You hear that?

00:35:22.204 --> 00:35:23.112
What?

00:35:33.978 --> 00:35:35.229
There's a door here.

00:35:38.609 --> 00:35:39.532
Dean.

00:35:44.938 --> 00:35:46.518
Step back from the door.

00:35:51.472 --> 00:35:52.818
Sam, put the gun down.

00:35:53.193 --> 00:35:54.351
Is that an order?

00:35:56.025 --> 00:35:57.699
That's more of a friendly request.

00:35:57.700 --> 00:35:59.999
'Cause I'm getting pretty
tired of taking your orders.

00:36:01.631 --> 00:36:02.726
I knew it.

00:36:03.321 --> 00:36:04.479
Ellicott did something
to you, didn't he?

00:36:04.480 --> 00:36:05.699
For once in your life,

00:36:06.122 --> 00:36:07.029
Shut your mouth.

00:36:07.030 --> 00:36:08.427
What are you gonna do, sam?

00:36:08.953 --> 00:36:10.696
The gun's filled with rock salt.

00:36:10.888 --> 00:36:11.920
It's not gonna kill me.

00:36:15.284 --> 00:36:15.910
No.

00:36:16.207 --> 00:36:17.115
But it'll hurt like hell.

00:36:25.108 --> 00:36:25.906
Sam.

00:36:26.531 --> 00:36:28.112
We've got to burn Ellicott's bones,

00:36:28.143 --> 00:36:29.520
And all this will be over,

00:36:29.885 --> 00:36:31.105
And you'll be back to normal.

00:36:31.277 --> 00:36:32.325
I am normal.

00:36:33.358 --> 00:36:34.969
I'm just telling the
truth for the first time.

00:36:35.470 --> 00:36:37.191
I mean, why are we even here?

00:36:37.989 --> 00:36:40.685
'Cause you're following dad's
orders like a good little soldier?

00:36:40.779 --> 00:36:43.297
'Cause you always do what
he says without question?

00:36:43.595 --> 00:36:45.597
Are you that desperate for his approval?

00:36:45.801 --> 00:36:47.240
This isn't you talking, Sam.

00:36:47.308 --> 00:36:48.904
That's the difference
between you and me.

00:36:49.123 --> 00:36:51.000
I have a mind of my own.

00:36:51.250 --> 00:36:53.018
I'm not pathetic like you.

00:36:53.019 --> 00:36:55.099
So what are you gonna do?
Huh. You gonna kill me?

00:36:55.146 --> 00:36:58.072
We're no closer to finding dad today

00:36:55.146 --> 00:36:58.072
You know, I am sick of
doing what you tell me to do.

00:36:58.562 --> 00:37:00.456
We're no closer to finding dad today

00:37:00.564 --> 00:37:02.395
Than we were six months ago.

00:37:04.277 --> 00:37:05.560
Well, then here.

00:37:05.810 --> 00:37:07.641
Let me make it easier for you.

00:37:09.831 --> 00:37:10.801
Come on.

00:37:10.989 --> 00:37:11.943
Take it.

00:37:12.297 --> 00:37:15.144
Real bullets are gonna work a hell
of a lot better than rock salt.

00:37:16.208 --> 00:37:17.100
Take it.

00:37:28.981 --> 00:37:30.483
You hate me that much?

00:37:32.110 --> 00:37:33.941
You think you can kill your own brother?

00:37:36.819 --> 00:37:38.164
Then go ahead.

00:37:39.385 --> 00:37:40.652
Pull the trigger.

00:37:47.011 --> 00:37:48.231
Do it!

00:38:05.773 --> 00:38:08.120
Man, I'm not gonna give
you a loaded pistol.

00:38:15.597 --> 00:38:16.833
Sorry, Sammy.

00:39:20.269 --> 00:39:21.739
Oh, that's just gross.

00:39:30.804 --> 00:39:31.884
Soak it up.

00:39:44.761 --> 00:39:46.170
Don't be afraid.

00:39:47.003 --> 00:39:48.396
I'm going to help you.

00:39:48.505 --> 00:39:50.336
I'm going to make you all better.

00:40:41.524 --> 00:40:43.386
You're not gonna try
and kill me, are you?

00:40:46.296 --> 00:40:47.125
No.

00:40:47.959 --> 00:40:48.815
Good.

00:40:50.196 --> 00:40:52.152
'Cause that would be awkward.

00:40:58.350 --> 00:40:59.492
Thanks, guys.

00:40:59.821 --> 00:41:01.010
Yeah, thanks.

00:41:01.401 --> 00:41:03.466
No more haunted asylums, okay?

00:41:10.894 --> 00:41:11.864
Hey, Dean.

00:41:13.256 --> 00:41:14.837
I' sorry, man. I

00:41:16.088 --> 00:41:17.950
said some awful thingsback there.

00:41:18.518 --> 00:41:19.785
You remember all that?

00:41:20.176 --> 00:41:21.037
Yeah.

00:41:22.727 --> 00:41:25.605
It's like I couldn't control
it, but I didn't mean it

00:41:26.012 --> 00:41:26.982
Any of it.

00:41:27.671 --> 00:41:28.625
You didn't, huh?

00:41:29.647 --> 00:41:30.664
No. Of course, not.

00:41:33.532 --> 00:41:35.112
Do we need to talk about this?

00:41:36.129 --> 00:41:37.005
No.

00:41:37.091 --> 00:41:39.868
I'm not really in the sharing
and caring kind of mood.

00:41:40.474 --> 00:41:42.023
I just want to get some sleep.

00:41:57.337 --> 00:41:58.197
Dean.

00:42:05.835 --> 00:42:06.695
Hello.

00:42:09.699 --> 00:42:10.419
Dad?



00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.000
